// CROWN refinement (P0·H, 2026-10-01): a pipe stage is an APPLICATION, so
// the stage's precondition claims of the piped value exactly as a call's
// does. `ratio` pipes `k + 1` — nothing proves it Positive — into `inv`,
// whose `n: Positive` guards the Trap of `100 / n`; the open claim pays that
// guard, so `ratio`'s `!Trap` refuses. On boot 13e8484a the pipe raised no
// claim at all: this checked clean and divided by zero. Expect
// E_EffectMismatch at ratio.
type Positive = Int where 0 < self

fn inv(n: Positive) = 100 / n

fn ratio(k) with !Trap = k + 1 |> inv

fn main() = ratio(0 - 1)
